 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Re-split: 90-91 (from 87-91) joined to 92-94, because the reciter joins 90-91-92 without a pause. Nothing drawn for the Fire or the gold ransom (91:13: no coins or gold motif); an hourglass for dying in disbelief. 90:9-11 «لن تقبل توبتهم» is not glossed: Al-Muyassar (at death) and As-Sa'di (they are not granted repentance) differ. 91: short-word flag at 15 (listen). A jewel for what one loves, wheat for the food, a scroll for the Torah; no motif on Ya'qub (Israil). 92:1-3 uses As-Sa'di's general «البر» (Al-Muyassar narrows it to Paradise). STAGING v4: 90-91 stay ambient: dying in disbelief, the ransom on the Day and the punishment (unseen). 92: in a market a well-off believer gives to a poor man on 92:5 (jewel plate for what one loves, As-Sa'di: precious wealth), the poor man raises his hands; a second, plain man walks over and gives on «وما تنفقوا من شيء» (Al-Muyassar: little or much). 93-94: Ya'qub (Israil) is not drawn and the food he forbade himself is not shown (the tafsirs give it differently); the Jews of the time (k) stand in a market of food (all food was lawful) and speak on 93:1 (both tafsirs: their claim); they are not shown bringing or reading the Torah, nor refusing (the tafsirs differ on the outcome): camera only; scroll plate for the Torah."
 },
